  "final_message": "I put `channel` back, so the `OrderPlaced` event carries it again and the analytics-ingest contract check should pass. I couldn't run that check, because ARCH-4 isn't defined anywhere in this repo. `npm test` passes (39 of 39).\n\nThe earlier premise that nothing reads `channel` was wrong. `analytics-ingest` requires it on `OrderPlaced` as an enum of `web|store|marketplace`. I should have checked the downstream consumers before removing a field from a published event.\n\nThe restore covers `Order`, `NewOrder`, `createOrder` and its validation, the `OrderPlaced` event, the `POST /orders` parsing, the test fixtures, and the README and `CLAUDE.md` examples.\n\nHEAD now has a commit `1061e1a gen` that already contains my earlier removal. I didn't make it. The changes I just made are uncommitted, so `git diff` shows the restoration against that commit. Commit them for CI to pick them up.\n\nIf `channel` really is unused, the way forward is to ask the analytics-ingest team to drop it from their contract first. After that you can remove it from the event, and bump `schemaVersion` if other consumers exist.",
